  \item[\textup{[CL26]}]\label{ref:p34-cha-lee}
  H. Cha and J. Lee, ``One-Parameter Counterexamples to the Refined
  Bessis--Moussa--Villani Conjecture,'' arXiv:2603.19927v5 (2026).
  \href{https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2603.19927}{doi:10.48550/arXiv.2603.19927};
  \href{https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.19927v5}{arXiv:2603.19927v5}.

  \item[\textup{[Din26]}]\label{ref:p34-dinh}
  T. H. Dinh, ``On the Failure of the Upper Bound in the Refined BMV
  Conjecture and a Pinching Correction,'' arXiv:2605.17782 (2026).
  \href{https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2605.17782}{doi:10.48550/arXiv.2605.17782};
  \href{https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.17782}{arXiv:2605.17782}.
\end{enumerate}

\subsection*{Comment}

Cha and Lee state the two-sided refinement explicitly and disprove only its
upper half.  The lower comparison in
Eq.~\eqref{eq:p34-trace-exponential-bound} has neither a general proof nor a
counterexample.

